  "goodToKnow": "Die Rentenversicherung is pension insurance. The statutory one, die gesetzliche Rentenversicherung, was introduced by Bismarck in 1889, among the first in the world. Today employers and employees each pay half of about 18.6 percent of gross salary, and it works on a pay-as-you-go basis (Umlageverfahren). Die Rente is a pension; rent for a flat is die Miete, a classic false friend. Plural: die Rentenversicherungen."
